{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a menorah.</b> To illuminate the table, as it is written: 'and he placed the menorah opposite the table.'" "<b>מקשה — it shall be made.</b> Rashi explained: because Moses was puzzled by it. And what he was puzzled about was its height, for it did not give a measurement for height as it did for all the other vessels of the Tabernacle." "<b>Its cups.</b> They are all fixed around the central shaft. When the oil drains down it goes into the first cup, and when the first fills it descends to the second, and from the second to the third, and from the third to that one in the body of the menorah, into which they all drain."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:30.751811584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}